IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dfa-fences`
IMPORT `dfa-qa`

-- Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (dfa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE
-- and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. These two groups are generated by the
-- scratchpad script gen_cases.py from the layer's own parameter lists.
--
-- Then each question is asked where its situation holds, with the answer worked by hand from the deposited text; for
-- each of the baseline's 13 exported questions (11 asked by the owner who wants the fence, s 13(3) by the owner asked
-- to pay and s 19 by the tenant), a case also asserts that the answer equals the baseline export's on the same facts.
-- The facts are HYPOTHETICAL (the baseline's own cases use none from the lives).
--
-- The situation inputs are BOOLEANs, so the "not read" cases cover them fully. The baseline reads `My interest in the
-- land`, `How the fence came to need repair`, `Reply to my repair notice` and `What I can recover for a repair` through
-- CONSIDER, some with OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31); for those, "not read" rests on the parameter script's check that
-- the role and the situation are read first. The layer's own helpers that turn the s 15 rule round list every value.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked role` IS A Role
ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked interest` IS A `My interest in the land`
ASSUME `an unasked cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair`
ASSUME `an unasked reply` IS A `Reply to my repair notice`
ASSUME `an unasked answer` IS A `What I can recover for a repair`
ASSUME `an unasked reply of mine` IS A `My reply to a repair notice`

`as the owner wanting the fence` MEANS `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired`
`as the owner asked to pay` MEANS `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence`
`as the tenant` MEANS `I rent land that a dividing fence borders`

