#ASSERT `Can I claim half the value of my fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `an unasked fact` TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `my claim` `not by s 13: I gave a notice to fence, so ss 9 and 10 apply`
#ASSERT `Can I claim half the value of my fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my claim` `no: the fence is not a sufficient fence (s 13(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim half the value of my fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my claim` `not yet: my neighbour has not built on, occupied or let a building on their land (s 13(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim half the value of my fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my claim` (`Can I claim half the value of the fence I built` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 15: a storm (repair at once, half, nothing else read); wear, notice, no reply after 15 days (half); 10 days (not yet);
-- a written dispute (the court); a fire through my neighbour's neglect they have not repaired (the whole).
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or accident, through nobody's neglect` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked number` `an unasked reply` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `I can recover` `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))`
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` FALSE TRUE 15 `no written reply` FALSE EQUALS `I can recover` `half: my neighbour did not reply within 14 days, so I may repair and recover half (s 15(7))`
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` FALSE TRUE 10 `no written reply` FALSE EQUALS `I can recover` `nothing yet: I must give a repair notice and wait 14 days for a written reply (s 15(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` FALSE TRUE 5 `disputes the need or objects to the repairs, in writing` FALSE EQUALS `I can recover` `the Magistrates Court decides: I may apply under s 15(4)`
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect` FALSE FALSE 0 `no written reply` TRUE EQUALS `I can recover` `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))`
#ASSERT `What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` TRUE TRUE 15 `no written reply` FALSE EQUALS `I can recover` (`What can I recover for repairing the fence` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` TRUE TRUE 15 `no written reply` FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much of the repair can I recover, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))` 800 EQUALS amount 400
#ASSERT `How much of the repair can I recover, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))` 800 EQUALS amount 800
#ASSERT `How much of the repair can I recover, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `the Magistrates Court decides: I may apply under s 15(4)` 800 EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of the repair can I recover, wanting the fence` `as the owner wanting the fence` `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))` 800 EQUALS amount (`How much of the repair cost can I recover` `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))` 800)
#ASSERT `May I enter my neighbour's land` `as the owner wanting the fence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I enter my neighbour's land` `as the owner wanting the fence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I enter my neighbour's land` `as the owner wanting the fence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I enter my neighbour's land for the fence work` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 19(1), the landlord's part: a 3-year tenancy (the whole), 6 years (three-fourths), 10 (one-half), 12 (none).
