-- s 15 against me. "My neglect" is mine: a fire through my neglect I have not repaired (the whole, s 15(8)); not yet
-- failed (I am bound to repair); a fire through my neighbour's neglect (they are bound); wear, notice, no reply after 15
-- days (half); I agreed in writing (half, my way); I disputed (the court, on my neighbour's application); no notice (not
-- yet); a storm (half at once, nothing else read).
#ASSERT `What can my neighbour recover from me for a repair` `as the owner asked to pay` `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect` FALSE FALSE 0 `I have not replied in writing` TRUE EQUALS `my neighbour can recover` `the whole: my neighbour may repair and recover the whole cost from me, as I have not repaired damage I am bound to repair (s 15(8))`
#ASSERT `What can my neighbour recover from me for a repair` `as the owner asked to pay` `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect` FALSE FALSE 0 `I have not replied in writing` FALSE EQUALS `my neighbour can recover` `nothing yet: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
#ASSERT `What can my neighbour recover from me for a repair` `as the owner asked to pay` `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked number` `an unasked reply of mine` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `my neighbour can recover` `nothing: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
#ASSERT `What can my neighbour recover from me for a repair` `as the owner asked to pay` `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` FALSE TRUE 15 `I have not replied in writing` FALSE EQUALS `my neighbour can recover` `half: I did not reply within 14 days, so my neighbour may repair and recover half from me (s 15(7))`
